          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Find the values of a and b for which the following system of equations has infinitely many solutions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.294,
            0.155,
            0.704,
            0.176
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_36_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "(a+b)x-2by=5a+2b+1;3x-y=14."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.187,
            0.882,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. Find the value of ‘k’ for which the following system of equations represents a pair of coincident lines:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.309,
            0.233,
            0.688,
            0.254
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_36_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "x+2y=3;(k-1)x+(k+1)y=k+3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.265,
            0.884,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. (i) Robot 1 starts from the origin and traces a path by repeatedly moving 3 units to the right and then 4 units upward. Robot 2 starts from the point (10, 0) and repeatedly moves 1 unit to the right and then 2 units upward. Will the paths traced by these two robots intersect and if so, where?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.366,
            0.884,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Robot 1 starts from (3, 0) and traces a path by repeatedly moving 5 units to the right and then 5 units upward. Robot 2 starts from the point (7, 0) and repeatedly moves 5 units to the right and then 3 units downwards. Will the paths traced by these two robots intersect and if so, where?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.468,
            0.884,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*12. At a certain time, Jacob notices that his digital watch reads ‘a’ minutes after two o’clock. Fifteen minutes later, it reads ‘b’ minutes after three o’ clock. He noticed that a is six times greater than b. What time was it when he looked at his watch for the second time?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.569,
            0.883,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*13. The sum of the digits of a two-digit number is 15. The number obtained by interchanging the digits exceeds the given number by 9. Find the number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.632,
            0.882,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*14. In a cyclic quadrilateral ABCD, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = (\\chi + 7)^{\\circ}, \\angle \\mathrm{B} = (y + 8)^{\\circ},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle C = (3y + 23)^{\\circ}   and   \\angle D = (4x + 12)^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find all four angles of the cyclic quadrilateral."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.696,
            0.883,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*15. A train moving with uniform speed for a certain distance takes 6 hours less if its speed is increased by 6 km/hour. It would have taken 6 hours more had its speed been decreased by 4 km/hour. Find the distance travelled and the speed of the train."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.777,
            0.884,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*16. The age of a father is equal to the sum of the ages of his four children. After 20 years, the sum of the ages of the children will be twice the age of the father. Find the age of the father."
            }
          ]
        }
